    "title": "Government revenue (General Revenue Account and the funds)",
    "tablenote": [
      "Financial year runs from 1 April to 31 March.  The investment incomes on the fiscal reserves for 2014-15 and 2015-16 have been set aside and retained within the Exchange Fund as provision for the Housing Reserve, and were not received on 31 December 2014 and 31 December 2015. The Housing Reserve was subsequently brought back to the Government’s accounts and recorded as investment income over four financial years from 2019-20 to 2022-23.",
      "The tax-loaded portion of fees and charges is re-classified under tax revenue.",
      "Figures have been adjusted to exclude proceeds from issuance of Government Bonds. The corresponding “Total capital revenue” and “Total government revenue” have been revised accordingly.",
      "[#7] The tax-loaded portion of fees and charges before 1995-96 are not available and the total amount of this item is put under other revenue.",
      "- Not applicable"
    ],
    "source": "Financial Services and the Treasury Bureau, Government Secretariat  For further information, please visit the website of the Financial Services and the Treasury Bureau, Government Secretariat (www.fstb.gov.hk).  (Enquiry telephone no.: 2810 3658   Enquiry e-mail : h_div@fstb.gov.hk)",
